# M4.26 read-only preflight probe diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-28

## Failure 1 — local wrapper interpolation

The first probe request failed inside the local JavaScript command wrapper with
`ReferenceError: name is not defined`. The SSH process was never started, so no
server command or mutation occurred. Cause: an unescaped shell variable inside
a JavaScript template literal. Resolution: escape the one interpolation point
and rerun the same read-only probe.

## Failure 2 — ambiguous first probe fields

The corrected broad probe completed, but three assumptions were wrong:

- it queried `tu1nz-adult-staging-s1.service` instead of the versioned
  `tu1nz-adult-publishing-s1.service`;
- it queried `tu1nz-backup.timer/service` instead of
  `tu1nz_encrypted_backup.timer/service`;
- it used `rg`, which is not installed on the server.

It also counted `information_schema.tables`, producing 40 instead of the
contractual 39 physical public tables. These ambiguous values were not used.

## Corrected evidence

A final read-only probe reused the exact M4.24/M4.25 unit names, the versioned
database snapshot implementation, `grep` where required, Git safe-directory
configuration and the full M4.25 release-gate argument set. It confirmed the
technical stopped boundary recorded in
`manifests/adult-publishing-commercial-first-start.m4-26.json`.

No probe started, restarted, enabled, stopped or reloaded a unit; wrote a file;
fetched or pulled Git; accessed secret values; activated a provider; or changed
the database.

## Draft-PR command wrapper

After the first M4.26 commit was pushed, the initial local Draft-PR command was
rejected by the JavaScript wrapper while parsing Markdown code delimiters. The
GitHub CLI was not invoked and no pull request was created by that attempt. The
same request was resubmitted without shell-sensitive Markdown delimiters and
created Draft PR #35 successfully. No branch rewrite or server action occurred.
